WEBVTT

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Companions and Prey</b>

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Companions and Prey</b>

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.510
Bisco, we're really going to freeze out here.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.520
There should be a camp of Shimobuki
 traders somewhere around here.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.750
Tough it out. Don't freeze until we find them.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.090
Easier said than done.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.500
What is it?

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.940
What's that smoke?

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.590
Not that. Look to the left of it.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:15.150
Huh?

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.270
A frostrabbit!

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.610
Leave it to me.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.630
Huh?

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.710
You think you can hit it 
with those frozen fingers?

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.700
You're just a city kid. Still wet behind the—

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:49.980
I used the synthesizer to mix 
boomshrooms and steelspider poison.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.730
I figured there had to be a way to land
 my quarry even if my arrows don't hit it.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.590
Did you follow that, Bisco-kun?

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.780
I don't accept this!

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.220
What's this?

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.320
Hey, it's that girl!

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.280
Well, our fates seem utterly entwined.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.500
Honestly, "fate" is the 
only way to describe it.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.890
Ten minutes later and 
you'd have been in trouble.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.470
You're always sticking your nose in.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.270
You must have a lot of time on your hands.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.080
Check out this attitude!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.400
Why can't you even say a word of 
thanks to the man who saved your life?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.340
Who would ever thank you?

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.890
Giving and receiving 
thanks is just a nuisance.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.680
I don't want to go around 
making ties or owing favors.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:45.940
Hey...

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.870
We traveled here as fast as we could.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.670
How'd you manage to get so far ahead of us?

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.540
I fixed up the helicopter stuck 
to that hermit crab temple.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.090
I was planning to make 
my way to Miyagi, but...

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:11.680
I got shot down by the anti-aircraft
gun in the Shimobuki base.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.590
Tsk, this is so lame.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:24.640
Things like that happen to you 'cause 
you live a life full of negative karma.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.690
Y'know, deceiving others and stuff.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.190
How else am I supposed to survive?

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.970
I've always done whatever it took to survive,

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.550
no matter how dirty or pathetic it was!

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.600
Even things you two children
could never dream of!

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.590
It's not like I chose a
 life of negative karma.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.030
I just did what I had to, 
and that's all there is to it.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.350
But I'm tired of it now.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.510
Maybe I'm done with trying 
to live this dull life.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:58.530
You don't mean...

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.750
That's why I keep saying 
you don't have to help me.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:06.040
If it weren't for you two, my life 
would've had a nice, neat ending.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.740
Hot!

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.070
Are you trying to kill me?! 
That's not something you do to a woman!

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.800
That ain't the reaction of 
someone who's given up on life.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.530
If you've got enough to spirit to bark 
like that, dying would be a waste.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.390
I only want Panda-kun 
to pay attention to me!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.820
You can go away!

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.440
Well, you heard her.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.320
We don't have many provisions, either.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.680
This just has our food and a stove.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.440
Um, uh...

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.190
We don't need your money!

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.940
Honestly, I'm just glad you're alive.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.680
We need to get going soon, though.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.540
Wh-Where to?

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.630
The subway. Shirakaba Line.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.840
Look, you...

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.290
Just get off!

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:09.100
Suck it up.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:14.090
It's warmer this way, and she said 
she'd guide us to the Shirakaba Line.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:16.840
Yup, that's right. <i>You</i> get off, punk!

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.730
I'm going with Panda-kun!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.840
Seems like you don't know 
how to show others respect.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.230
I saved your life, dumbass!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:33.120
See? You made Actagawa mad.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.900
There, there.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:40.040
Crab?

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.220
Crab!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:40.860
Crab!

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.130
What'd he say?

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.090
We can't use sols.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:57.260
They want blankets, liquor, and other 
stuff from before the Tokyo explosion.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.590
Like we'd have any of that 
stuff! We're not salvagers.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.350
Huh?! W-We can't do that!

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:08.680
What now?

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.640
He said he's a fine crab.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:14.830
If we give them Actagawa, they'll give 
us cloaks or anything else we want.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.710
These bastards! Who'd be dumb 
enough to sell their own family?!

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:20.070
You said it.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:24.390
Don't let these Shimobuki Traders buy him.
They have no intention of doing business.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:25.100
Huh?

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.890
Hey, don't butt in.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.090
I'm a trader, too.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.130
Here's some advice.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.260
They're goody-goodies.
Give them a good deal to earn their trust and swindle them later.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.550
See how dumb they are?

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.930
Thanks to them, I've bought 5 homes!

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.180
Earn their gratitude now, and the returns will be huge!

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:43.750
Bisco, this woman's amazing, huh? She's so fluent.

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.080
You'll regret that, fish-paste woman.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.080
Huh? Why?

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.460
I don't know why, but I get 
the feeling she was mocking us.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.200
What are you, an animal?

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.080
I don't believe it.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.520
Some dried giant eel is enough
 for them all of a sudden?

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.220
What kind of magic did you use?

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.460
It's a secret.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:02.580
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:02.710
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.350
You even got them to throw this in as a bonus.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:02.830
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:02.960
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

