<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:03.580
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:03.710
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:03.830
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:03.960
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:04.080
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:04.210
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:04.330
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:04.460
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:04.580
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:04.710
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:04.830
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:04.960
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:05.210
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:05.330
<b>Field Guide to Life
in Konakidani</b>

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.240
Don't even ask, Milo. You know
she used some dirty trick.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.210
Knowing will only sully your spirit.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.370
Then take that pure spirit of 
yours and freeze to death!

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.930
Take it off! Take the cloak off right now!

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.970
This is Kitsunezaka Station.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.930
The entrance has frozen over.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.810
That's no problem for us.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.420
Actagawa.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.430
Wow, pretty!

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.410
Glowshrooms.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.350
Their only flaw is they're not all that bright.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:57.910
So these spores sprout on walls,
 but putting them in your mouth is fine?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.550
There's a trick to it.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:01.380
Who do you think I am—

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.880
You haven't figured out the trick, have you?

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:09.590
Shut up. It's every little thing with you.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.770
Look, Bisco.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.700
<b>Xinghao</b>

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:22.910
<b>Xinghao</b>

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.450
<b>Xinghao</b>

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.410
Xinghao...

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.290
<b>Xinghao</b>

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:30.420
<b>Juntong</b>

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.150
Juntong, Zhenfeng...

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.410
They're all trains from Huabei Ironworks.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:34.060
Trains like these should be self-operated.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.460
Assuming they still work, that is.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:37.890
Hey, Milo!

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.320
Amazing! This one might actually run.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:47.700
According to Kousuke's map, 
it's on the right line, too.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.430
Let's see... Place the lever 
in the designated position...

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.620
Put in the 300-yen fare,
 and press the red button?

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.150
That's so damn expensive.

00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:59.380
Oh, well...

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.440
What?! Yen?!

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.330
There's no way we have that! 
We don't trade in old coins!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.330
<b>Please deposit fare here</b>

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.330
<b>Yen</b>

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.330
<b>Boarding Ticket</b>

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.330
<b>Passenger Ticket</b>

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:05.870
Aw, jeez.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:05.580
<b>Matoba</b>

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:05.580
<b>Manu</b>

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:05.580
<b>facturing</b>

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:07.640
Outta the way.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.320
I can't watch this.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.450
Seriously...

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:19.500
I see. Just gotta get this part to move, huh?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.380
You understand how 
these old machines work?

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.600
I just worked as a mechanic 
in my previous job.

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:28.600
Previous job? You mean you 
used to work for a company?

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:33.980
I was basically treated like a slave 
back then, but the pay wasn't bad.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:39.100
Though, one day, we got put in charge of
 repairing an excavated part of Tetsujin.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:43.470
I don't know if it was the real deal, 
but we were ordered to restore it.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:45.790
By the famous Matoba Manufacturing.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.800
Sounds crazy, doesn't it?

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.110
But they were serious.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.090
The factory workers Rusted
to death one after another.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.610
Once I'd made it from the bottom
 rung all the way up to forewoman,

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:00.020
I ran for my life.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.430
That was a long time ago, though.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:09.110
This slipshod construction 
makes it hard to tweak.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.390
Give me some time, okay?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:20.390
It's been a while since we just 
relaxed and enjoyed a meal.

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:24.290
We couldn't help it. We didn't 
exactly have time to stand around.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:28.300
I didn't know anything about 
what it was like outside the walls.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:34.160
I could've easily been ground out 
by one badly-timed gust of wind.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:39.190
Don't worry. Once this journey's over and you 
save your sister, you can go back to city life—

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.430
That's not what I mean, Bisco!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.430
That's not it.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:44.960
I've had fun.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.010
It was all so pretty.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.960
The scenery, the air, the water...
Even that huge shrimp temple.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:55.190
How should I put it? They were 
all teeming with the power of life.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:12:00.090
What did I see in all that 
time I spent in Imihama,

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.710
where the city walls blocked my view?

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:08.570
While the city offered me protection, 
it was putting those kids through awful fates.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.740
Dummy. You're overthinking things.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.070
You did everything you could 
there as a doctor, right?

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:21.830
Not everyone could've saved as 
many lives as you did in that place.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.350
Even I had my hands full 
trying to save just one old man.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.210
Is Jabi-san your mentor?

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:34.640
Well, how should I put it? 
He's kind of a mentor, kind of a father...

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:36.480
But...

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.470
Jabi's just Jabi.

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:41.110
He taught me all kinds of things.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.980
How to use a bow. How to survive.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:49.650
Back in the day, he was as strict as a demon, 
and I practically died several times over.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:51.650
Jabi-san was like that?

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.490
So many times, I thought,

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:57.910
"The first thing I'm gonna do once 
I'm stronger than him is beat him up."

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:04.290
Still, that damn old man is my one and only...

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.080
damn old man.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.260
I want to save him.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:15.970
We'll save him.

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:19.200
We'll save Jabi-san, Bisco.

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:23.810
You're the top star of the Mushroom 
Keepers, and I'm a doctor.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.380
If we put our heads together, then...

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.560
Well, of course.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:34.940
We're saving them. 
Both Jabi and your older sister.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.390
Is it okay for me to speak up now?

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.710
You're done already?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.330
Yeah, a good while ago.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:47.290
And thanks to that, I heard everything.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:49.860
Th-Thank you.

00:13:50.230 --> 00:13:51.510
Eat lots.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:14:00.020
Hey, how are you able to risk your life
 and go so far for someone else?

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:07.070
Probably because I love her.

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:11.980
Also, because I'm not very cunning.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.940
You're both idiots. Seriously.

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:26.950
Dryworm.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.960
Giant woodpecker.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.920
Scorched shrike.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:33.770
Hmm, that's not it.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:37.010
What kind of field guide is this, anyway?

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.980
Are these a kid's sketches?

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:42.470
They were drawn by a Mushroom Keeper.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:43.900
You can tell?

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.060
It has a unique style to it, right?

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:48.250
That's the Mushroom Keepers' special touch.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:50.010
Jabi draws like that, too.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:52.360
Does it have mushroom varieties in it?

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:57.000
Like which ones come from which 
creatures. Like cloud ear or shimeji.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.750
<b>Scorched
Shrike</b>

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.750
<b>Shiitake</b>

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:58.730
Is this it?

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:01.520
You're right. There's 
something on every page.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.380
<b>Rust
\hEater</b>

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.130
<b>Rust
\hEater</b>

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:06.140
"Rust Eater."

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.500
Bisco, this is it! The pipe snake.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.080
Common name: tube worm.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:16.380
It can fly, and it often eats large prey
 such as helicopters and fighters.

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:20.390
All Jabi told me was that it's on 
the biggest thing around here.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.610
So having that makes a big difference.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:23.340
Yeah.

00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.920
Wow! It's really running!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.930
This is as far as I go.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.400
Your journey sounds fun, 
but without life, there's nothing.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:44.030
I want to thank you, but you 
haven't even told us your name.

00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:48.050
It's fine, don't worry about it.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:51.230
I'm Milo. Nekoyanagi Milo.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.300
This scary guy here is Akaboshi Bisco.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:58.550
If it wasn't for you, we might've perished here.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.060
Please, tell us your name.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.600
J-Jellyfish is fine.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:08.570
I-I don't tell people my name, 
because everyone always laughs at it.

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:11.170
We both have odd names ourselves.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:13.950
It'll be fine. We won't laugh.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:22.190
T-Tirol.

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.580
Oochagama Tirol.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:26.960
Thanks, Tirol.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.580
You saved us.

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:34.290
You were right. We should've asked her name 
sooner, since there's a thread of fate linking us.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:39.690
If you'd croaked on your travels, I wouldn't 
have known what to put on your gravestone.

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:42.610
Oh, shut up! You two are 
gonna die before me!

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:45.740
If I find either of your corpses, 
I'll bury you upside-down!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.270
Thank you, Tirol.

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:56.060
I'm truly glad we met.

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:00.890
Tirol, I'm sure we'll meet again!

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:03.960
We'll talk about you a lot.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:07.320
We'll always be thinking of you, wondering 
where our friend is and what she's up to!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:10.330
F-Friend?

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.090
Tirol!

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:17.970
Let's meet again someday!

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:26.180
A-Akaboshi! Milo!

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.210
Th-Thank...

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:34.770
Thank you.

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:45.500
<b>Pipe
\h\h\h\hSnake</b>

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:45.500
<b>Rust
\h\hEater</b>

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:44.550
What should we do about the "big prey" 
we need to catch a pipe snake?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:51.620
Oilsquid!

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.600
We must've passed their nest somewhere.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:00.690
Only aim for the ones jumping at us!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.500
Bisco, I can't use a bow yet!

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:04.270
You can!

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.940
You can shoot. You can hit them.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:10.750
I know you can.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:12.780
I'm leaving you to watch my back.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.650
Bisco...

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:16.070
Gonna answer me?!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:16.890
Yes, sir!

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.070
Here they come!

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.500
Well done.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.930
There's no end to them.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:38.200
We've got no choice. It'll mean we 
can't go back home this way, but...

00:18:45.080 --> 00:18:46.540
What is this?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.010
Silver acid nameko.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:50.570
Don't breathe too much of it in. Get down!

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.880
We did it. Bisco, they stopped chasing us.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.800
Seriously, every time. That odor's rank.

00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:06.950
Bisco!

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:12.580
Bisco!

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.700
Shit! They had a leader!

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.930
Bisco!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:27.230
The exit...

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.890
It's too far.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:30.700
Actagawa!

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:32.970
Rip out the engine!

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:33.930
Hurry!

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:37.620
Into that thing's mouth!

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:54.220
Now, if I shoot through that...

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:01.690
There are just two rules for using a bow.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:04.680
Rule one: keep your eye on the target.

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:07.130
Rule two: believe in yourself.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:10.900
Will you hit it?

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:12.180
Yeah.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.670
Bisco, this is...

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.290
Yeah. Weeping Child Ravine.

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:41.780
It's pretty, but it seems 
like a lonely place, too.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.110
Look, mushrooms!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:48.050
Then this blue smoke is...

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:53.930
Spores. Mushroom Keepers came 
here and harvested the Rust Eater.

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:55.730
Fifteen years ago.

00:20:57.280 --> 00:20:58.110
Milo!

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.000
A b-bird?!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:10.940
That's it! The pipe snake!

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:12.470
That's way too huge!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:16.200
There's no way that's a snake! It's a dragon!

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:22.590
Bisco!

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:24.800
We'll target it from both sides!

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.090
I told you not to be reckless—

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.610
Actagawa!

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.750
Shit... How do we do this?

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.610
Akaboshi!

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.120
Talk about the worst possible timing.

00:21:49.310 --> 00:21:50.610
Pawoo?!

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.450
Divine punishment shall be swift!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:37.220
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:37.220
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:29.310
Obtaining the sacred mushroom, Rust Eater, 
is what every Mushroom Keeper hopes to do.

00:23:29.310 --> 00:23:31.310
They're all quite capable, too.

00:23:31.310 --> 00:23:33.800
But the true enemy is people, Bisco.

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.290
Next episode: "The Stolen Rust Eater."

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:39.380
What? It's gonna be stolen?

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>The Stolen Rust Eater</b>
